{"event_index": 9, "event": "proposal_response", "at_utc": "2026-11-05T05:37:34.639375+00:00", "candidate_id": "c0001", "stage": "init_01", "generation": 0, "generation_order": 1, "prompt": "Solving a black-box combinatorial optimization problem via stochastic solution sampling following \"heuristics\".\nSuppose `n` represents the scale of the problem. The heuristics function takes as input a `node_attr` array of shape (n,) and a `node_constraint` integer as a certain constraint imposed on the item attributes. The heuristics function returns a `heuristics` array of shape (n, n). `heuristics[i][j]` indicates how promising it is to group item i and item j.\nFunction interface: def heuristics_v2(node_attr: np.ndarray, node_constraint: int) -> np.ndarray:\nPropose a new heuristic without an existing heuristic.\nReturn exactly <thought>algorithm description</thought> followed by <code>the complete executable Python module, including import numpy as np and def heuristics_v2(node_attr: np.ndarray, node_constraint: int) -> np.ndarray:</code>. Do not use tools or read files. No other text or Markdown fences.", "response": "<thought>Use a capacity-aware complementarity heuristic: pairs that fit together receive higher scores when their combined size approaches the constraint, while infeasible pairs receive zero. A mild balance term favors pairing items of different sizes, and normalization makes scores comparable across instances.</thought><code>import numpy as np\n\n\ndef heuristics_v2(node_attr: np.ndarray, node_constraint: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Estimate how promising it is to group each pair of items.\"\"\"\n    values = np.asarray(node_attr, dtype=float).reshape(-1)\n    n = values.size\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return np.empty((0, 0), dtype=float)\n\n    capacity = float(node_constraint)\n    if not np.isfinite(capacity) or capacity <= 0:\n        return np.zeros((n, n), dtype=float)\n\n    values = np.nan_to_num(values, nan=capacity, posinf=capacity, neginf=0.0)\n    values = np.maximum(values, 0.0)\n\n    pair_sum = values[:, None] + values[None, :]\n    feasible = pair_sum <= capacity\n\n    utilization = np.clip(pair_sum / capacity, 0.0, 1.0)\n    tightness = utilization ** 2\n\n    scale = max(capacity, float(np.max(values)), 1.0)\n    size_difference = np.abs(values[:, None] - values[None, :]) / scale\n    balance = 1.0 - np.clip(size_difference, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    scores = tightness * (0.65 + 0.35 * balance)\n    scores *= feasible.astype(float)\n\n    np.fill_diagonal(scores, 0.0)\n\n    maximum = float(np.max(scores))\n    if maximum > 0.0:\n        scores /= maximum\n\n    return scores.astype(float, copy=False)\n</code>"}
